# Bring-up of the Nexus 5X (bullhead-halium) on the 16.0 GSI, added by 65-extra-init.
#
# lmkd crashed four times before boot completed, and as a critical service that made init
# reboot, which in the container means stopping it. Let it fail instead, so the rest can
# come up and be looked at (init honours this on a debuggable build, which the GSI is).
on early-init
    setprop init.svc_debug.no_fatal.lmkd true

# Keep Android's own log on disk (/data/misc/logd in the container,
# /data/android-data/misc/logd on the phone): the container dies with it otherwise.
on post-fs-data
    setprop persist.logd.logpersistd.buffer all
    setprop persist.logd.logpersistd logcatd

# The vendor's init.bullhead.sensorhub.rc declares flash-nanohub-fw without a user, which the
# Android 16 init rejects ("No user specified for service 'flash-nanohub-fw', so it would have
# been root"), so "start flash-nanohub-fw" on post-fs failed with "service not found" and the
# sensor hub was never brought to the firmware in /vendor/firmware/nanohub.full.bin. The hub
# then answered no reads (nanohub_kthread err_cnt every second from boot on), the sensors HAL
# listed nothing and sensorfwd restarted every few seconds (10 Oct 2026). The same service,
# with the user Android 6 ran it as; nanoapp_cmd only flashes when the version differs.
service flash-nanohub-fw /vendor/bin/nanoapp_cmd download
    user root
    group system
    oneshot
    disabled
